    <briefdescription>
<para>Placeholder metadata for operands of distinct MDNodes. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This is a lightweight placeholder for an operand of a distinct node. It&apos;s purpose is to help track forward references when creating a distinct node. This allows distinct nodes involved in a cycle to be constructed before their operands without requiring a heavyweight temporary node with full-blown RAUW support.</para>
<para>Each placeholder supports only a single <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_m_d_node" kindref="compound">MDNode</ref> user. Clients should pass an <ref refid="namespacellvm_1_1_calling_conv_1abdf8cf606905c10634e831390981b0ed" kindref="member">ID</ref>, retrieved via <emphasis><ref refid="classllvm_1_1_distinct_m_d_operand_placeholder_1a629021baa296713fdc2ab0c208904d16" kindref="member">getID()</ref></emphasis>, to indicate the &quot;real&quot; operand that this should be replaced with.</para>
<para>While it would be possible to implement move operators, they would be fairly expensive. Leave them unimplemented to discourage their use (clients can use std::deque, std::list, <ref refid="namespacellvm_1a8e612822d4ba7bb36c9c79582a567108" kindref="member">BumpPtrAllocator</ref>, etc.). </para>
    </detaileddescription>
